# Reports: framework started

`Backend/reports/` now exposes three builders:

- `build_patent_vs_infringement_report(case_id, infringement_id)`
- `build_products_patents_infringements_report(case_id, hit_kind=...)`
- `build_whats_new_report(user_id, folder_id=...)`

Flask download routes are wired:

- `GET /api/report/single-infringement/<case_id>/<infringement_id>?kind=product|patent`
- `GET /api/report/all-infringements/<case_id>?kind=product|patent`
- `GET /api/report/latest-updates/<folder_id>` (`unsorted` allowed)

Still pending when the user asks what's next on reports:

- Live verification against real case data (broader than the laser-diode smoke previews)
- Optional: stamp `created_at` on infringement writes for reliable “what's new”
